<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # I Can Make a Mola. – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Beautiful Mola</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I Can Make a Mola.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Respond in writing to written questions from peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can compose simple personal letters about mola art (e.g., 'Dear Juan Carlos, I like the colorful molas.'). Can respond to peers' written questions about molas (e.g., 'What colors were used?' 'The mola is red and blue.'). Can revise letters or responses for clarity and correctness (e.g., add 'colorful' to describe the mola).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays various pictures of molas, including those with turtles, butterflies, and jaguars, and asks students to quickly point and name colors and animals. Students then do a quick "Think-Pair-Share" to say one thing they like about a mola (e.g., "I like the vibrant colors."). This activates prior vocabulary from previous lessons.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a simple sentence on the board describing a mola, like: "I like this mola because it has a golden turtle." The teacher explicitly models how to write a complete sentence, pointing out the subject, verb, and the subordinating conjunction 'because' for giving a reason. The teacher also spells out words like 'mola' and 'colors', emphasizing the /m/ and /k/ sounds for phonemic awareness.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the word 'because' for? Is it for saying what you don't like or why you like something?" (Expected answer: "Why you like something.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I write a sentence, does it start with a big letter or a small letter?" (Expected answer: "A big letter.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Beautiful Mola".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Short, simple written exchanges in the form of a 'Mola Question & Answer Board' (e.g., student-written questions and possible responses). The genre is informal written communication (peer questions, simple responses), using a friendly register.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will learn to interpret and respond in writing to simple questions about mola art, describing things and expressing preferences in written form.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Actions:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher displays a few examples of written questions and written answers on the board or projector, e.g.:
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; padding-left: 20px;">Q: "What colors were used in your mola?"</p>
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; padding-left: 20px;">A: "The mola is red and blue. It also has a unique butterfly."</p>
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; padding-left: 20px;">Q: "Why do you like to decorate molas?"</p>
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; padding-left: 20px;">A: "I like to decorate because it shows my creativity."</p>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher highlights the use of the Present Simple ("The mola is...") and the conjunction 'because'. Also, key vocabulary like 'colors', 'decorate', 'creativity', 'unique', 'butterfly'.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students match the questions to their correct answers on a worksheet.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students identify two colors mentioned in the answers and circle them.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences using Present Simple, the subordinating conjunction 'because', and vocabulary related to mola art (nouns: mola, creativity, project, inspiration, culture, turtle, butterfly, jaguar; verbs: cut, sew, paste, choose, express, illustrate, decorate, collaborate; adjectives: turquoise, golden, round, vibrant, traditional, unique; adverbs: carefully, skillfully, artistically, also; conjunctions: and, because; sequence: first, second, third, next, last). Spelling of one- and two-syllable words (e.g., 'red,' 'second') for phonemic awareness is also practiced.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1 (Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher provides sentences with blanks. Students complete the sentences using target vocabulary and grammar structures. Example: "I like this ________ because it has a _________ jaguar." or "A mola has _________ and _________ colors." (Writing focus: filling in words correctly).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2 (Semi-controlled - Guided Sentence Construction):</b> The teacher shows pictures of different molas or mola-making steps. For each picture, students write two sentences: one describing it using Present Simple, and one expressing a preference using 'I like... because...'. Example: "Picture: A mola with a green turtle." Student writes: "The mola has a green turtle. I like the green turtle because it is vibrant." (Writing focus: composing sentences from prompts).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3 (Pair Writing & Peer Check):</b> Students work in pairs. Each student writes three simple written questions about molas or mola-making steps (e.g., "What colors do you choose?" "First, do you cut the fabric?" "Why do you like mola culture?"). They then exchange their questions with their partner. Each partner reads the questions and writes short, simple answers in complete sentences. After writing, they exchange papers again and check for capitalization, periods, and if the target vocabulary (e.g., 'turquoise,' 'skillfully') is used correctly. (Writing focus: generating questions, responding in writing, and revising for correctness).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Beautiful Mola".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Written product – Students compose simple personal letters/responses to their peers about mola art. The scenario is 'Responding to a Pen Pal about Molas'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Actions:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are paired up. Each student receives a 'pen pal letter' (pre-written or from another student's previous work, or from Activity 3) containing 2-3 simple written questions about their mola project or mola preferences (e.g., "Dear [Name], What colors were used in your mola? Do you like the round shapes?").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students write a response letter addressing each question. They must use the Present Simple, 'because' for reasons, and incorporate at least three vocabulary words from the list (e.g., 'vibrant', 'creativity', 'traditional', 'cut', 'sew', 'illustrate', 'jaguar', 'turtle'). They are encouraged to describe their mola and express preferences.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example structure: "Dear [Peer's Name], Thank you for your letter! My mola is red and turquoise. It has a beautiful butterfly. Yes, I like the round shapes because they are unique. I like to decorate my mola skillfully. Best, [Your Name]." (Writing focus: composing a coherent written response).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in written expression, collaborative interaction (through written exchange), and communicative task completion (responding to all questions). Students practice acknowledging peers' contributions and sharing feedback in written form.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer Assessment Checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their written response letters from the Production stage. They use a simple checklist to evaluate their peer's letter, providing written feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Peer Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: square; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did the letter answer all the questions? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did the letter use 'because' to explain a reason? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did the letter use at least three mola vocabulary words? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are most words spelled correctly (especially 1-2 syllable words like 'red', 'second')? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is it clear and easy to understand? (Yes/No)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket (written):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new mola word you used today in your writing?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing your letter was easy? What was difficult?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection (written):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did I learn about writing about molas today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I use 'because' to give reasons in my next writing project?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., Peer checking helped students identify common errors, clear examples provided good scaffolding for letter writing.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., Provide more sentence starters for lower-level writers, dedicate more time to pre-writing brainstorming for vocabulary usage.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How did students manage the writing task? (e.g., Most students successfully responded to questions and used 'because', but some struggled with spelling longer vocabulary words.)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration):</b> In the next lesson, students will use their accumulated knowledge and writing skills to integrate and summarize information about molas for a 21st Century Skills Project, possibly creating a simple informational poster or presentation, building on their ability to describe, explain, and express preferences in a structured way.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">3 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>